                <head>557. Notes of the Secretary of State’s Staff Meeting, Department of State,
                    September 9, 1957, 9:15 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d557-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1957-09-09T09:15:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 9, 1957,
                                9:15 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>[Here follow a list of those present (23), an intelligence briefing, and
                    discussion of matters unrelated to Uruguay.]</p>
                <p>8. <hi rendition="#italic">Uruguay</hi>—Mr. Rubottom said he was extremely
                    discouraged over the poor political situation in Uruguay which is drifting into
                    a potentially dangerous trend. He characterized this as one of extreme
                    complacency, an unsound overdoing of the welfare state and a dangerous
                    penetration of the government by Leftists and Communists. He noted mounting
                    anti-US feeling.</p>
                <p>[Here follows discussion of matters unrelated to Uruguay.]</p>
            </div>
